    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25-a1">

                <pb facs="0100" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg30"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Van Valkenburgh</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 27, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    letter of the 26th October, and of the first of a bill of exchange for £2,673
                    12s. <hi rendition="#italic">2d.</hi> at six months, drawn in my favor by the
                    Oriental Bank at Yokohama on the Union Bank, London, which I shall place in
                    proper course of collection, on account of the foreign department of the
                    government of the United States, as heretofore directed in former cases.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. B. Van Valkenburgh,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States, Yedo,
                            Japan.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
